title: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › The exceptions
route: /authorizations/eligibility/V-1001
intro: A check can end with a warning that needs a look. There are eight, and each says what was found and what to do next. The warnings sit in one quiet block under the three parts of the result, and in step 2 of New Case. A warning never forces anyone to abandon a case, and none of them is a payer decision: they report what the check found.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: every one can be reached. Three have a seeded patient on the list (R-1101, R-0975, R-1118) and each has a chip on Verify, under 'Try a sample' or 'More samples'. 'Verification service unavailable' happens when Verify is paused in Settings.
---
start s1 "A check finishes with something to look at"
decision q0 "Which warning?"

group gW "The eight warnings"
  process x1 "Coverage is not active\nCoverage lapsed or ended on a date before the service\nNext: ask the payer, or request retro-eligibility\nSeeded: R-1101 (lapsed), R-0975 (ended)"
  process x2 "The payer changed\nThe member is with another plan since a date. Start the request with the new plan\nSeeded: R-0975 (now Cardinal since 10/01)\nChip: 'Payer changed'"
  process x3 "Member ID does not match\nNo member matched, or the plan has the member under another ID. Read the card again\nChips: 'Not found', 'Member ID mismatch'"
  process x4 "Benefit not confirmed\nThe plan answered for coverage but not for this service. Caller can confirm by phone\nChip: 'Benefit not confirmed'"
  process x5 "Service not covered\nThe plan does not cover this level of care. Ask which program it pays for\nSeeded: R-1118. Chip: 'Not covered'"
  process x6 "Provider participation not confirmed\nThe clinic's enrollment could not be confirmed. Navigator can check the enrollment record\nChip: 'Provider not confirmed'"
  process x7 "Verification service unavailable\nVerify is paused in Settings, so nothing was asked. Resume Verify, then refresh"
  process x8 "Authorization requirement unknown\nNo rule on file for this payer and level of care. Check with the payer. Nothing was assumed\nChip: 'Requirement unknown'"
endgroup

screen sc "One quiet block under the result, one line each:\n'Coverage is not active. Coverage ended 09/30. Ask the payer, or request retro-eligibility; ...'"
screen sn "New Case step 2 shows the same block in its summary, and the case can go on\nWarnings are saved with the draft"
decision q1 "Is the warning 'Verification service unavailable'?"
process p1 "A known patient keeps the last result, marked with the warning, check time unchanged\nAnyone else shows 'Not checked' everywhere"
click c1 "Click 'Check again' (result) or 'Refresh verification' (New Case)"
process p2 "Still paused: toast 'Could not re-check ...' and the last result stays\nResumed: the check runs and the warning goes"
process p3 "The verdict follows: 'Fix before billing', 'Authorization first' or 'Not checked'\nThe sidebar badge counts it until it is cleared"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Result › Which verdict and why"
goto g2 "Continues in: Authorizations › Eligibility & Benefits › Verify › More samples: checks that need a look"
goto g3 "Continues in: Authorizations › New Case › How a case starts and resumes"
goto g4 "Continues in: Settings"

s1 --> q0
q0 -->|Any of the eight| x1 & x2 & x3 & x4 & x5 & x6 & x7 & x8
x1 & x2 & x3 & x4 & x5 & x6 & x8 --> sc
x7 --> q1
q1 -->|Yes| p1 --> c1 --> p2
x7 -.-> g4
sc --> p3 --> g1
sc --> sn --> g3
q0 -.-> g2
